      "title": "String Interpolation",
      "lectureOrder": 347,
      "videoOrder": 324,
      "sourceHash": "b3a577ecfabccf2ef847a28f9af1bf6be2f47617a81fe923db70a674bb54c751",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.55,
          "end": 4.65,
          "en": "-: Let's start by having a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.65,
          "end": 6.42,
          "en": "at string interpolation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.42,
          "end": 9,
          "en": "Here in The Server Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 11.73,
          "en": "I don't want to output this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.73,
          "end": 13.08,
          "en": "in the html code like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.08,
          "end": 15.72,
          "en": "I don't want to hard code the output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.72,
          "end": 17.49,
          "en": "It would be realistic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.49,
          "end": 20.1,
          "en": "that our server component contains information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.1,
          "end": 22.2,
          "en": "about a specific server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 24.93,
          "en": "So, maybe here in the template file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.93,
          "end": 29.19,
          "en": "we want to output \"Server with ID\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.19,
          "end": 32.433,
          "en": "and then some dynamic ID here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.637,
          "end": 37.05,
          "en": "\"is\", and then the status like \"offline\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.05,
          "end": 39.363,
          "en": "So, we have two dynamic fields here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.23,
          "end": 42.51,
          "en": "Now, it would makes sense to kind of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.51,
          "end": 44.43,
          "en": "derive them in TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.43,
          "end": 46.29,
          "en": "In a real app, that might be derived",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.29,
          "end": 48.695,
          "en": "from http request you make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.695,
          "end": 51.99,
          "en": "to some backend or some calculation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.99,
          "end": 54.72,
          "en": "For now, I will hard code it in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.72,
          "end": 57.237,
          "en": "So, we might have a \"serverId\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.74,
          "end": 61.23,
          "en": "and I will assign a value of, let's say, 10.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.23,
          "end": 62.373,
          "en": "So, a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 63.3,
          "end": 65.913,
          "en": "and I might also have a \"serverStatus\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.08,
          "end": 69.75,
          "en": "which is a string \"offline\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.75,
          "end": 73.47,
          "en": "So, two different types, a string and a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.47,
          "end": 75.21000000000001,
          "en": "And, though not necessary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.21000000000001,
          "end": 77.43,
          "en": "you could also be very explicit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.43,
          "end": 78.63,
          "en": "by assigning the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.63,
          "end": 80.07,
          "en": "with type scripts feature here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 80.07,
          "end": 82.2,
          "en": "of adding a colon after the property name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 82.2,
          "end": 83.73,
          "en": "and then the type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 83.73,
          "end": 85.65,
          "en": "It will infer it automatically, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 85.65,
          "end": 87,
          "en": "so, this is not required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 87,
          "end": 90,
          "en": "I'm just doing this here for demo purposes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 90,
          "end": 91.47,
          "en": "So, now I want to output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 91.47,
          "end": 94.35,
          "en": "these two properties in my template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 94.35,
          "end": 95.628,
          "en": "And, to get this connection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 95.628,
          "end": 97.28999999999999,
          "en": "we need to update data binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 97.28999999999999,
          "end": 98.12299999999999,
          "en": "because you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 98.12299999999999,
          "end": 99.27000000000001,
          "en": "it's all about the communication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 99.27000000000001,
          "end": 102.24000000000001,
          "en": "between your type's root code and template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 102.24000000000001,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "So, string interpolation is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 105.72,
          "en": "a typical use case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 105.72,
          "end": 108.57,
          "en": "or typical solution for this task here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 108.57,
          "end": 111.18,
          "en": "Instead of the placeholder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 111.18,
          "end": 113.37,
          "en": "I use my double curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 113.37,
          "end": 114.6,
          "en": "opening and closing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 114.6,
          "end": 116.75999999999999,
          "en": "This is the string interpolation syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 116.75999999999999,
          "end": 120.57,
          "en": "And, in between these double curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 120.57,
          "end": 124.71,
          "en": "you can now write a TypeScript expression.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 124.71,
          "end": 126.36,
          "en": "So, the easiest expression is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 126.36,
          "end": 129.33,
          "en": "to simply reference a property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 129.33,
          "end": 131.31,
          "en": "like the \"serverId\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 131.31,
          "end": 133.29,
          "en": "And, this is a common use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 133.29,
          "end": 136.89,
          "en": "that you only output property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 136.89,
          "end": 139.23,
          "en": "or the value of the property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 139.23,
          "end": 142.5,
          "en": "However, it's not the only use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 142.5,
          "end": 146.43,
          "en": "You could also, for example, here for \"server\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 146.43,
          "end": 148.74,
          "en": "simply hard code a string in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 148.74,
          "end": 151.59,
          "en": "Any expression which can be resolved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 151.59,
          "end": 153.09,
          "en": "to a string in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 153.09,
          "end": 155.19,
          "en": "That's the only condition for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 155.19,
          "end": 157.82999999999998,
          "en": "a string interpolation syntax here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 157.82999999999998,
          "end": 160.71,
          "en": "So, whatever you have between the curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 160.71,
          "end": 163.59,
          "en": "in the end, it somehow has to return a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 163.59,
          "end": 165.32999999999998,
          "en": "So, you could also call a method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 165.32999999999998,
          "end": 167.043,
          "en": "which returns a string in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 167.88,
          "end": 169.95,
          "en": "The only other restriction is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 169.95,
          "end": 172.82999999999998,
          "en": "you can't write multi-line expressions here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 172.82999999999998,
          "end": 175.29,
          "en": "You can't write block expressions in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 175.29,
          "end": 178.076,
          "en": "so, you can't add a \"if\" or a \"for\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 178.076,
          "end": 180.42,
          "en": "control structure in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 180.42,
          "end": 183.39,
          "en": "You could use a ternary expression, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 183.39,
          "end": 186.12,
          "en": "So, this is what you can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 186.12,
          "end": 188.97,
          "en": "Now, let's also replace the last placeholder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 188.97,
          "end": 190.14,
          "en": "And, here, I will again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 190.14,
          "end": 191.73,
          "en": "just reference a property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 191.73,
          "end": 193.283,
          "en": "the \"serverStatus\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 194.13,
          "end": 197.694,
          "en": "Now, this is string interpolation in usage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 197.694,
          "end": 199.86,
          "en": "and you see that we have expression,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 199.86,
          "end": 201.3,
          "en": "which is a string itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 201.3,
          "end": 202.71,
          "en": "and then two other expressions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 202.71,
          "end": 205.02,
          "en": "which simply point to properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 205.02,
          "end": 207.15,
          "en": "And again, you could also call a method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 207.15,
          "end": 208.59,
          "en": "which returns a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 208.59,
          "end": 210.18,
          "en": "Now, interesting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 210.18,
          "end": 213.63,
          "en": "the \"serverId\" is not a string, but a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 213.63,
          "end": 216.24,
          "en": "And, I just said that string interpolation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 216.24,
          "end": 219.45,
          "en": "has to resolve to a string in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 219.45,
          "end": 221.94,
          "en": "has to get a string in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 221.94,
          "end": 223.59,
          "en": "So, let's see if this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 223.59,
          "end": 226.86,
          "en": "If we save this with ng serve still running,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 226.86,
          "end": 228.84,
          "en": "let's also change \"app-server\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 228.84,
          "end": 232.11,
          "en": "back to \"app-servers\" to make this work again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 232.11,
          "end": 235.11,
          "en": "We see 'Server with ID 10 is offline\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 235.11,
          "end": 236.01,
          "en": "We see it twice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 236.01,
          "end": 237.66,
          "en": "because we repeat this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 237.66,
          "end": 238.71,
          "en": "and each component, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 238.71,
          "end": 239.94,
          "en": "has the same content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 239.94,
          "end": 243,
          "en": "but we see that string interpolation is working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 243,
          "end": 246.99,
          "en": "and that it especially is also working here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 246.99,
          "end": 249.03,
          "en": "for our number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 249.03,
          "end": 250.32,
          "en": "So ID 10.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 250.32,
          "end": 251.64,
          "en": "That is not an issue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 251.64,
          "end": 253.08,
          "en": "That is working fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 253.08,
          "end": 257.01,
          "en": "because a number can be easily converted into a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 257.01,
          "end": 259.164,
          "en": "So yes, you have to get a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 259.164,
          "end": 262.53,
          "en": "in the end or something which can be converted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 262.53,
          "end": 265.77,
          "en": "to a string to really be correct here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 265.77,
          "end": 268.35,
          "en": "This is how you can use string interpolation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 268.35,
          "end": 270.6,
          "en": "And, now, to really complete the example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 270.6,
          "end": 273.24,
          "en": "let's say the server status here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 273.24,
          "end": 275.587,
          "en": "somehow returned in a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 275.587,
          "end": 278.88,
          "en": "\"getServerStatus\" could be the method name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 278.88,
          "end": 281.55,
          "en": "This is how you define a method in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 281.55,
          "end": 283.08,
          "en": "So, you might note this kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 283.08,
          "end": 285.63,
          "en": "of method definition from other languages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 285.63,
          "end": 289.5,
          "en": "And, here, we simply \"return this.serverStatus\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 291.39,
          "end": 293.13,
          "en": "So, we return the property here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 293.13,
          "end": 294.79200000000003,
          "en": "We could, of course, have accessed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 294.79200000000003,
          "end": 297.6,
          "en": "it directly, as we already did,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 297.6,
          "end": 300.36,
          "en": "but just to demonstrate that you can call a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 300.36,
          "end": 302.677,
          "en": "Here, I am calling a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 302.677,
          "end": 305.49,
          "en": "\"getServerStatus\" of course leads",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 305.49,
          "end": 307.59,
          "en": "to the same output, because again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 307.59,
          "end": 310.47,
          "en": "all this method does is it returns us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 310.47,
          "end": 312.24,
          "en": "a string in the end or something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 312.24,
          "end": 314.07,
          "en": "which can be converted to a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 314.07,
          "end": 316.953,
          "en": "That is string interpolation in action.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
